  "limitations": [
    "The number of included studies was relatively small due to strict inclusion criteria (randomized controlled designs).",
    "Several included studies used small samples, leading to less stable effect size estimates.",
    "Most studies assessed emotion at a single point in time directly after exposure to nature, limiting understanding of long-term effects.",
    "All studies were conducted in developed industrialized nations, limiting generalizability to other cultures or developing nations.",
    "The review focused exclusively on emotional components of well-being, not other facets of well-being.",
    "The relative lack of studies on specific positive emotions precluded quantitative comparisons.",
    "Methodological issues regarding the specific natural environments used (often resource-rich) may bias findings towards positive affect."
  ],
